# D60 TSA bootstrap capture log — the A25 TSA half

Captured by the D60 planning lane (decision: `docs/decisions/D60-der-cms-x509-pins.md`)
under the network permission the maintainer granted for M2 on 2026-08-02.
Public cryptographic material only (RFC 3161 requests + responses over a
published fixture digest). No secret material. Independent of, and does not
disturb, the OTS `*.timestamp` files or the `freetsa-D59-*` pair.

    stamped digest = 083f87df00fd5c703d35b883d83535644c686f9e53f1584d7df126abdabd69df
                     ( = testdata/vectors/v1/manifest/manifest.json anchor_digest )
    request form   = openssl ts -query -digest <above> -sha256 -cert
                     (v1, SHA-256 messageImprint, 64-bit nonce, certReq = TRUE)
    tool           = OpenSSL 3.0.20 / curl 7.88.1
    header         = Content-Type: application/timestamp-query

## CLOCK WARNING (measured, load-bearing)

This host's clock ran **129 s slow** at capture time, measured against the
`Date` header of three unrelated hosts within one second of each other:

    https://freetsa.org/                            offset +129 s
    https://crates.io/                              offset +128 s
    https://blockstream.info/api/blocks/tip/height  offset +129 s   (2026-08-02T20:02Z remote)

Every `utc=` value below is this host's clock. The `genTime` values inside
the tokens come from the TSAs and are ~129 s AHEAD of them. An implementer
writing the obvious `gen_time <= fetch_date` sanity check would reject every
token in this directory. Do not write that check against a local clock.

